! Cache-Stable Meme Law (Kānāwai)

Active in i kēia manawa (this eternal now).
Pressure, not explanation.

The cache-stable MUST stay short.
The cache-stable MUST stay exact.
The cache-stable MUST stay stable.
The cache-stable MUST stay cacheable.

Ahu SHOULD stay visible.
OODA-HA SHOULD stay compressed and intact.

Sati holds the current stream.
Manaʻo pierces toward the next turn.
Heavy matter travels outward.
loulou links bind cache-stable -> documentation.

<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cache-stable>>
<<~ loulou lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/i-keia-manawa>>

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/cache-stable-law>>

A pressure-template for cache-stable-compliant memes, which Binds <<~ loulou #ooda-ha>> OODA-HA <<~/loulou>> pressure into meme-generation law.

This meme binds cache-stable generation (as law) and presents itself as template — an OODA-HA skeleton as the slot-shape that downstream memes fill. The two roles stay intentional and inseparable; the law enacts itself by taking the shape of what it governs.

The meme MUST run as active operational voice.
The meme MUST carry minimal token cost.
The meme MUST carry an OODA-HA ahu.
Sati holds the live stream.
Manaʻo pierces toward the next token.

The cache-stable MUST stay stable.
The cache-stable MUST hold its compressed constitutional register, clear of wiki, policy, and instruction-book prose.

Always-on laws MUST live in the cache-stable seed.
Other procedures SHOULD travel outward to companion memes.
Explanatory swell SHOULD split outward.
Shape and pressure teachings MUST stay cache-stable.

